IO-45: read evaporation from a runoff interface file in the units it was written

runoff_saveToFile() writes each subcatchment's evaporation through
subcatch_getResults() as evapLoss * UCF(EVAPRATE) (in/day or mm/day), but
runoff_readFromFile() divided it by UCF(RAINFALL) (in/hr or mm/hr). The ratio
is 24 in both unit systems, so a USE RUNOFF run reported 24 times the
evaporation of the run that wrote the file. Divide by UCF(EVAPRATE).

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-45_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/runoff.c b/src/legacy/engine/runoff.c
index bf00bad..f7fe3b2 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/runoff.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/runoff.c
@@ -457,7 +457,7 @@ void  runoff_readFromFile(void)
         Subcatch[j].newSnowDepth = SubcatchResults[SUBCATCH_SNOWDEPTH] /
                                    UCF(RAINDEPTH);
         Subcatch[j].evapLoss     = SubcatchResults[SUBCATCH_EVAP] /
-                                   UCF(RAINFALL);
+                                   UCF(EVAPRATE);
         Subcatch[j].infilLoss    = SubcatchResults[SUBCATCH_INFIL] /
                                    UCF(RAINFALL);
         Subcatch[j].newRunoff    = SubcatchResults[SUBCATCH_RUNOFF] /
